* This is an example of a sine stimulus from a first order delta sigma modulator.
.model comparator dac_bridge(out_low = -2.5 out_high = 2.5 t_rise=1ns t_fall=1ns) 
*athresh_comparator [%vd threshold control] [over_threshold] comparator
asinestim [dac_out] [drv_out] comparator
asinestim2 [pwm_low] [drv_out_l] comparator
asinestim3 [pwm_high] [drv_out_h] comparator

* A tiny Verilog module handles the deltaSigma dac and test bench.
.model vlog_ds d_cosim simulation="ivlng" sim_args=["../src/sine_stim_test"]
averilog null [ dac_out pwm_low pwm_high] vlog_ds

* output rc filter
Lf drv_out filt_out 10u
cout filt_out 0 470n
RL filt_out 0 8
.end
.options trtol=8 reltol=0.005
.control
tran 10n 2m 
*fourier v(filt_out) 2k
*plot pwm_out-5 drv_out2-10 filt_out
plot drv_out_h drv_out_l-5
*linearize v(filt_out)
*linearize v(drv_out2)
*set specwindow=blackman
*fft v(filt_out)
*fft v(drv_out2)
*plot db(mag(v(filt_out))) ylimit -100 20
*plot db(mag(v(drv_out2))) xlog xlimit 1000 1Meg ylimit -100 20
write output_data.raw
.endc
